[0.000, "o", "d charge and returned a 400 from the provider. It now voids the\n\u001b[5Gauthorisation instead, with a test for both cases.\r\n  \u001b[35;1mYou\u001b[m\n\bShip it behind a flag.\r\n  \u001b[34;1mClaude\u001b[m\n\u001b[5GAdded `checkout_v2` to `flags.yaml`, off by default. The old handler stays the fallback until the flag\n\u001b[5Gis removed."]
[2.201, "o", "\r\u001b[4A\u001b[J\u001b[5d  \u001b[33m●\u001b[m \u001b[36m6f1c2a9e-3b7d-4e21-9a55-0c8e7d1b4f62\u001b[m  \u001b[90m15/11/2026 15:56\u001b[m  \u001b[90m381.9K\u001b[m  \u001b[33m✎ Checkout rewrite\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[35;1m▌\u001b[m   \u001b[36mb2d84f17-90ce-4a3b-8e6f-5d21c7a9e034\u001b[m  \u001b[90m15/11/2026 13:02\u001b[m  \u001b[90m 57.7K\u001b[m  \u001b[1m  Fix flaky cart tests\u001b[m\u001b[18;6H\u001b[90mpreview · p hides · P moves ─────────────────\u001b[m\n\n\u001b[5Gcart_test.go fails one run in five on CI\u001b[K\n\n\u001b[5GThe tests share a package-level `clock`. Each test now gets its own `fakeClock`, and `-count=50`\n\u001b[5Gpasses.\u001b[K"]
[1.300, "o", "\r\u001b[J\u001b[6d    \u001b[36mb2d84f17-90ce-4a3b-8e6f-5d21c7a9e034\u001b[m  \u001b[90m15/11/2026 13:02\u001b[m  \u001b[90m 57.7K\u001b[m    Fix flaky cart tests\r\n\u001b[35;1m▌\u001b[m   \u001b[36me7a03c55-1f2b-4d8e-b6c9-2a4f80d7e1b3\u001b[m  \u001b[90m14/11/2026 14:02\u001b[m  \u001b[90m143.5K\u001b[m  \u001b[1m  Add Stripe webhooks\u001b[m\u001b[20;5Hhandle stripe webhooks for refunds\u001b[K\n\n\u001b[5GAdded `/webhooks/stripe` with signature checks and idempotency keys stored in `webhook_events`.\u001b[K"]
[1.316, "o", "\r\u001b[6d\u001b[35;1m▌\u001b[m   \u001b[36mb2d84f17-90ce-4a3b-8e6f-5d21c7a9e034\u001b[m  \u001b[90m15/11/2026 13:02\u001b[m  \u001b[90m 57.7K\u001b[m  \u001b[1m  Fix flaky cart tests\u001b[m\r\n    \u001b[36me7a03c55-1f2b-4d8e-b6c9-2a4f80d7e1b3\u001b[m  \u001b[90m14/11/2026 14:02\u001b[m  \u001b[90m143.5K\u001b[m    Add Stripe webhooks\u001b[20;5Hcart_test.go fails one run in five on CI\n\n\u001b[5GThe tests share a package-level `clock`. Each test now gets its own `fakeClock`, and `-count=50`\n\u001b[5Gpasses."]
[0.400, "o", "\r\u001b[5d\u001b[35;1m▌\u001b[m \u001b[33m●\u001b[m \u001b[36m6f1c2a9e-3b7d-4e21-9a55-0c8e7d1b4f62\u001b[m  \u001b[90m15/11/2026 15:56\u001b[m  \u001b[90m381.9K\u001b[m  \u001b[33;1m✎ Checkout rewrite\u001b[m\r\n    \u001b[36mb2d84f17-90ce-4a3b-8e6f-5d21c7a9e034\u001b[m  \u001b[90m15/11/2026 13:02\u001b[m  \u001b[90m 57.7K\u001b[m    Fix flaky cart tests\u001b[18;6H\u001b[90mrunning: busy (pid 3978) · p hides · P moves \u001b[m\n\n\u001b[5GDoes the refund path still work when capture failed?\n\n\u001b[5GNo. `Refund` assumed a captured charge and returned a 400 from the provider. It now voids the\u001b[K\n\u001b[5Gauthorisation instead, with a test for both cases.\r\n  \u001b[35;1mYou\u001b[m\n\bShip it behind a flag.\r\n  \u001b[34;1mClaude\u001b[m\n\u001b[5GAdded `checkout_v2` to `flags.yaml`, off by default. The old handler stays the fallback until the flag\n\u001b[5Gis removed."]
